            <ArticleTitle>Combined PTCA and microcoil embolization of a left internal mammary artery graft.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>141-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Internal mammary arteries are increasingly common conduits for coronary revascularization. Although infrequent, cardiologists are faced with a number of technical failures. We describe a case of combined PTCA to a LIMA insertion stenosis, along with coil embolization of a large unligated intercostal side branch. A complication of embolization is described along with angiographic follow-up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
